Sorry, this sat two years without a single reply. That is on us.

I have rebased it on 8.2 and finished it. `getAllowedAttributes()` was restructured since by the wildcard fix (3759838b4a2), so the change is ported rather than replayed:

* the exclusion is a separate condition, so ignored beats allowed whichever groups are requested;
* the "no restriction" short-circuit at the end now also requires no ignored groups. Without that, passing only `IGNORED_GROUPS` returned `false` and every attribute was serialized, which your third test case covers;
* added `AbstractNormalizerContextBuilder::withIgnoredGroups()`, which every other context option has, with a test;
* moved the CHANGELOG entry to the 8.2 section and fixed the Branch row.

Your tests apply unchanged and pass. Serializer is green (1430 tests), PropertyInfo too (662).

One known limitation for reviewers: `SerializerExtractor::getProperties()` carries the twin of this check but is driven by its own `serializer_groups` context key, so it does not honour ignored groups. Adding that means introducing a `serializer_ignored_groups` key in PropertyInfo, which is a separate decision and out of scope here.
